ired a physical copy.\n  - actors: Joanna watched a classic movie that had a gripping story and great actors.\n  - sci-fi movie: Joanna asked Nate if he has a favorite sci-fi movie after discussing video games.\n  - story: Joanna's movie story explores loss, redemption, and forgiveness, and features elements of self-discovery. Nate noted it was about a turtle, highlighting its inspiring resilience.\n  - watching movies: Joanna enjoys watching movies as a hobby, in addition to writing, reading, and exploring nature.\n  - the last one: Joanna is inspired to write a story about a thirty-year-old woman on a self-discovery journey after a loss, similar to 'the last one'.\n  - movies: Joanna highly rates movies (9-10/10) for emotional impact. Nate suggested watching one of Joanna's movies together.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - it: Joanna found seeing characters/dialogue she wrote acted out to be an amazing, rewarding experience; this is the third time this has happened. Nate is excited to watch it.\n  - things to watch: Nate told Joanna he will give her a shout whenever he runs out of things to watch.\n  - big screen: Joanna is writing a movie script, a love story with challenges, hoping to get it on the big screen.\n  - movie reccomendations: Joanna is willing to give movie recommendations, which Nate usually likes more than random movie choices.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script, finding every day on set awesome and full of potential while showing her vision.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - script: Joanna is filming a movie from her road-trip script. An actor praised the script, making Joanna excited and giving her chills.\n  - acting: Joanna enjoys acting, especia